 | `CONFIG_MDC1200` | n | MDC-1200 PTT ID on FM channels (`core/mdc`, `docs/spec/radio-features.md` 3.8): a channel sends its ID when a transmission starts, ends or both, and can decode the IDs it receives. Needs APRS_AFSK: the burst goes out through the AFSK sender and borrows its idle transmit buffer, and the decoder borrows the idle APRS demodulator's memory (APRS_RX for decoding). Off unless built with `CONFIG_MDC1200=y` |
 | `CONFIG_APRS_IGATE` | = APRS_RX and HOSTLINK (n where flash is short) | the iGate rules, RF to APRS-IS and messages back, with the host helper `tools/aprs_gate.py` holding the APRS-IS connection |
 | `CONFIG_DMR` | y | DMR voice: modem driver, call stack, AMBE FEC, vocoder hosting, PCM audio |
